* SprintStart - Project Overview

- Purpose :: AI-assisted onboarding tool for companies
  - Build a knowledge base using RAG from multiple sources
  - Users can ask questions about the knowledge base
  - System generates knowledge-specific onboarding paths for new hires

- Architecture :: Split across 3 projects
  ** Frontend :: Web application (likely React)
  ** Backend :: Kotlin + Spring Boot (we are here)
  ** AI :: RAG pipeline, embeddings, LLM orchestration (likely Python)

- This file :: /home/fabian/Desktop/git/sprintstart-backend

* Backend Module Overview

- Source root :: src/main/kotlin/com/sprintstart/sprintstartbackend/
- Test root :: src/test/kotlin/com/sprintstart/sprintstartbackend/

- Modules (by package):
  ** connectors/ :: Data source integrations (GitHub, Jira)
  ** ingestion/ :: Artifact ingestion pipeline
  ** chat/ :: Chat over knowledge base
  ** onboarding/ :: Onboarding paths, phases, steps, blueprints
  ** user/ :: User management, Keycloak integration
  ** upload/ :: Document upload & processing
  ** insights/ :: Knowledge gaps & FAQ generation
  ** shared/ :: Shared utilities (web clients, crypto, scheduling)
  ** health/ :: Health check endpoint
  ** config/ :: Security, CORS, Keycloak config

* Tech Stack

- Kotlin
- Spring Boot
- Spring Modulith
- Spring Data JPA / Hibernate (PostgreSQL)
- Gradle Kotlin DSL
- JUnit 5 / MockK / Mockito Kotlin
- Keycloak for auth
- Docker Compose for local infra
